      "text": "nor the servant above his lord, Matt. 10:24 (John 13:16; 15:20). Behold my servant, whom I have chosen, Matt. 12:18. certain king, which would take account of his servants, Matt. 18:23. chief among you, let him be your servant, Matt. 20:27 (23:11; Mark 10:44). Who then is a faithful and wise servant, Matt. 24:45 (JS—M 1:49). Blessed is that servant, whom his lord when he cometh shall find so doing, Matt. 24:46 (JS—M 1:50). Well done, thou good and faithful servant, Matt. 25:21. first … shall be last of all, and servant of all, Mark 9:35. We are unprofitable servants, Luke 17:10. thou good servant: because thou hast been faithful in a very little, Luke 19:17. Whosoever committeth sin is the servant of sin, John 8:34. where I am, there shall also my servant be, John 12:26. servant is not greater than his lord, John 13:16 (15:20). These men are the servants of the most high God, Acts 16:17. Paul, a servant of Jesus Christ, Rom. 1:1 (Philip. 1:1; Titus 1:1). to whom ye yield yourselves servants to obey, Rom. 6:16. made myself servant unto all, 1 Cor. 9:19. thou art no more a servant, but a son, Gal. 4:7. Servants, be obedient to … your masters, Eph. 6:5 (Col. 3:22; Titus 2:9–10; 1 Pet. 2:18). servants … count their own masters worthy, 1 Tim. 6:1. servant of the Lord must not strive, 2 Tim. 2:24. faithful in all his house, as a servant, Heb. 3:5. James, a servant of God and … Jesus Christ, James 1:1. not using your liberty for a cloak of maliciousness, but as the servants of God, 1 Pet. 2:16. Simon Peter, a servant … of Jesus Christ, 2 Pet. 1:1. they themselves are the servants of corruption, 2 Pet. 2:19. Jude, the servant of Jesus Christ, Jude 1:1. shew unto his servants things which must shortly come to pass, Rev. 1:1. Hurt not the earth … till we have sealed the servants of our God, Rev. 7:3.",
